From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:25:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: publish the SMC's
 other temperature channels

The J604's SMC updates about 150 readable temperature keys that no J604
devicetree file lists, next to the 44 the board files already name.

Add them from the same macOS 26B123 key sweep: readable 4-byte floats
that moved between two reads 20 s apart on an idle desktop and read as
a temperature there (10-120 C; one key at 4 C is left out). They are
labelled "SMC <key>", since which part of the machine each one watches
is not mapped on this machine. A key the running SMC firmware does not
offer is skipped by the driver.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../dts/apple/t8132-j604-hwmon-rails.dtsi     | 759 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 755 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hwmon-rails.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hwmon-rails.dtsi
index 3b01bbfcc2..b966f82990 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hwmon-rails.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hwmon-rails.dtsi
@@ -1,10 +1,11 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+ OR MIT
 /*
- * T8132 J604 power, voltage and current channels published by the SMC.
+ * T8132 J604 power, voltage, current and temperature channels published by the SMC.
  *
- * Every readable float power, voltage and current key the J604's SMC updates on an idle macOS
- * desktop (macOS 26B123 key sweep: flt, 4 bytes, flags 0x85, value moving
- * between two reads 20 s apart) that the common laptop files do not list.
+ * Every readable float power, voltage, current and temperature key the
+ * J604's SMC updates on an idle macOS desktop (macOS 26B123 key sweep:
+ * flt, 4 bytes, flags 0x85, value moving between two reads 20 s apart)
+ * that the common laptop and board files do not list.
  * Only the backlight's consumer is proven on this machine: PBLR follows the
  * panel content and level (about 0.28 W on a full black and 2.2 W on a full
  * white window at the same level, 6.6 W at a high level). The other keys
@@ -479,4 +480,754 @@ current-Ib8f {
 		apple,key-id = "Ib8f";
